From: Donnie Guedry <dguedry@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Device-level surfaces, virtual surfaces and Direct2D rendering devices.

On top of wine-staging 11.17 (patch set dcomp-DCompositionCreateDevice2):

- keep the rendering device a composition device is created with, and route
  IDCompositionDevice::CreateSurface / CreateVirtualSurface through a surface
  factory on it;
- virtual surfaces: ordinary surfaces plus Resize (a new backing surface, content
  not carried over) and Trim (no-op);
- a Direct2D rendering device: the factory obtains the DXGI device behind it
  (ID2D1Device2::GetDxgiDevice) for surfaces and copies, and BeginDraw can hand
  out an ID2D1DeviceContext targeting the draw surface;
- EndDraw no longer refuses non-DXGI factories.

Makes Steinberg's graphics2d-based products (HALion Sonic 7) run: they create the
composition device from a Direct2D device, draw through ID2D1DeviceContext and use
virtual surfaces. Verified 2026-09-26, HALion Sonic 7.5 standalone renders fully.

